// The thing whose jungle this is.
//
// **A resident, not a boss**, and the distinction is the tone gate
// (`DECISIONS.md` §8): the jungle is not a target gallery and this is
// not a health bar with a name on it. It is what has been living here
// the whole time, and it comes out when a tower has made enough noise
// in its home that ignoring the tower stops being an option.
//
// **It is also the only reason to stand and fight.** §11 makes walking
// away the free answer to every wave, which is right — and a free
// answer with no alternative is not a decision. A mother is slow enough
// to walk away from and carries enough that you might not. That is the
// whole of what it adds.
//
// What it carries is not loot. It is what a very large thing that has
// been pulling apart machines for years turns out to have in it.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
EnemyDef(
    id: "enemy.thicket_mother",
    name: "Thicket Mother",
    glyph: "🕷",
    // Half again a mire-hulk's 340, and the largest number in the pack
    // by a distance. A dart battery needs thirty-four hits; a lone
    // thorn gun would need sixty-three and run the tower out of bamboo
    // first. It is not shot down by an emplacement — it is shot down by
    // a *tower*, which is the shape of encounter this exists to make.
    hp: 500,
    // Slow, like everything large here. You see it a long way off and
    // the decision it poses is made at leisure: walk, or commit.
    speed_paces_per_100_ticks: 9,
    // Hits harder than anything else, on a long cycle. A mother that
    // reaches the hull takes a room apart rather than scratching it.
    damage: 26,
    attack_ticks: 85,
    // Long, but not a hulk's 3000: this can be walked away from, and
    // that has to stay true or the alternative stops being a choice.
    cling_ticks: 1500,
    approach: Ground,
    // The most expensive thing a wave can field. At
    // threat_per_100_provocation 40 a budget of 60 needs provocation
    // 150 — well past the point where a run has been noticed.
    threat: 60,
    min_provocation: 420,
    // Region 1. The jungle's own resident, met in the jungle, which is
    // the opposite of the mire-hulk's "the coast is not impressed by
    // you" — this is "you are in somebody's home".
    min_region: 0,
    // **What it leaves.** Alloy, which otherwise needs a salvage rig, a
    // forge and a ruin to stop at — so felling one is a genuine
    // shortcut through a whole chain rather than a pile of the material
    // you already have. Two of them: enough to matter, not enough to
    // replace the chain.
    drops: [
        CostEntryDef(item: "item.alloy", amount: 2),
        CostEntryDef(item: "item.scrap", amount: 8),
    ],
)
